  "passage": "My grandmother has sold vegetables at the same market for nearly forty years, and last Sunday she let me help her (1)____ the first time. We left the house while it was still dark. (2)____ the time we reached the market, the lorries from the countryside had already arrived and men were carrying boxes of cabbages on their shoulders. Grandma greeted everyone (3)____ name. She has known most of the other sellers since they were children, and they clearly respect her. My job was simple: I had to arrange the tomatoes in neat rows (4)____ the best ones were at the front. By seven the first customers appeared. (5)____ of them were mothers who wanted to finish their shopping before work. One woman argued about the price for nearly five minutes, but Grandma just smiled and gave her an extra chilli. \"If you (6)____ her leave unhappy, she won't come back,\" she told me afterwards. At nine o'clock a boy on a motorbike delivered a basket of fresh herbs (7)____ smell filled the whole corner. I had never noticed how loud a market is: bells, radios, people calling out prices, and somewhere a rooster that would not stop. By eleven there was hardly (8)____ left on the table, and my feet hurt so much that I could barely stand. Grandma, (9)____ is seventy-two, did not look tired at all. She counted the money, gave me a note for my help and said I could come again (10)____ I promised not to eat the strawberries next time.",
