  "passage": "We moved house in July, and I still have not (1)____ used to the new flat. For twelve years I had lived in the same room, with the same view of the same mango tree, and I did not want to leave. My parents, (2)____, were excited. The new place is closer to their offices and has a lift, which matters (3)____ my grandfather cannot manage stairs any more. The packing took two whole weeks. Mum wrote the name of a room on every box, but by the end nobody was paying attention, and the kitchen knives ended (4)____ in a box marked 'bathroom'. On moving day the lorry arrived an hour late, and the driver refused to carry the piano (5)____ we paid him extra. My father was furious, but there was nothing he could do. The strangest moment came when the old flat was completely empty. Our voices sounded different, and the walls had pale squares (6)____ the pictures used to hang. I took one last photo and closed the door. Since then I have slowly been getting to know the neighbourhood. There is a bakery downstairs, a park (7)____ five minutes' walk of our building, and a boy next door who plays the same online game as me. Last week I finally (8)____ round to unpacking my books, and the room started to feel like mine. My old friends have promised to visit, though I know that promises like that are not always (9)____. Still, Mum says that by next summer I will wonder (10)____ I ever made such a fuss.",
